00:59:26.240 --> 00:59:27.120
Perfectly preserved.

00:59:27.830 --> 00:59:29.190
And I think I know why.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:31.300
Because it was filled in that cave?

00:59:32.960 --> 00:59:35.300
No, not exactly.

00:59:36.150 --> 00:59:38.670
Do you remember the vapor that shot up out of the hole

00:59:38.670 --> 00:59:40.350
when we tried the stone tablet loose?

00:59:40.470 --> 00:59:41.310
Do I, I'll say.

00:59:41.470 --> 00:59:43.090
I thought we'd had it right then.

00:59:43.730 --> 00:59:46.810
I believe that some ancient tribe buried this mummy,

00:59:47.540 --> 00:59:51.740
not just thousands of years ago, but hundreds of thousands.

00:59:53.410 --> 00:59:54.410
They were very primitive.

00:59:55.380 --> 00:59:57.360
Their writings and pottery work show that.

00:59:58.180 --> 00:59:59.980
And yet these people had found the secret.

01:00:00.030 --> 01:00:01.970
of truly preserving the dead.

01:00:02.940 --> 01:00:03.520
But how?

01:00:04.720 --> 01:00:07.800
They combined certain amounts of various woods and resins

01:00:07.920 --> 01:00:09.840
that were present on the earth at that time.

01:00:10.750 --> 01:00:12.750
They put them in those earthen vessels we found

01:00:12.750 --> 01:00:14.290
and burned them in a sealed cave.

01:00:15.130 --> 01:00:17.450
The smoke and the incense have the power of preserving

01:00:17.450 --> 01:00:18.650
whatever was in the cave.

01:00:19.290 --> 01:00:22.210
So that's why the jars we found were filled with ashes.

01:00:22.760 --> 01:00:26.090
That vapor that escaped from the cave was a preservative smoke,

01:00:26.550 --> 01:00:27.910
hundreds of thousands of years old.

01:00:28.160 --> 01:00:29.200
Well, that's my theory.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.280
Could very easily be wrong, though.

01:00:31.720 --> 01:00:33.560
Hey, it moved.

01:00:34.360 --> 01:00:34.880
